        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": "Since these are different quantities, we need to have distinct ways of writing them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.124,
            0.848,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": "To identify the place value where integers end and the fractional parts start, we use a point or period (‘.’) as a separator, called a **decimal point**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.18,
            0.681,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "The above quantities in decimal notation are then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.209,
            0.844,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "| Quantity | Decimal Notation |\n| --- | --- |\n| 7 hundreds and 5 ones(700 + 0 + 5) | 705 |\n| 7 tens and 5 tenths (70 + 0 + 1 50) | 70.5 |\n| 7 units and 5 hundredths(<sup>7</sup> <sup>+</sup> <sup>0</sup> <sup>+</sup> 1 500) | 7.05 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_16_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.439,
            0.824,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": "These numbers, when shown through place value, are as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.469,
            0.838,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "| Decimal number | Hundreds | Tens | Units | Tenths | Hundredths |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 705 | 7 × 100 | 0 × 10 | 5 × 1 |  |  |\n| 70.5 |  | 7 × 10 | 0 × 1 | 5 ×1 10 |  |\n| 7.05 |  |  | 7 × 1 | 0 ×1 10 | 5 ×1 100 |",
